(begin-tx "DALOS-G2a — GAS_PAYER: the payable form IS funded")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DALOS-G2a · 01 · the happy path] ---")
;;GAS_PAYER is the capability the Ouronet gas station acquires before agreeing to pay for a
;;transaction, and it is the most commercially exposed guard family in DALOS: everything it
;;rejects is a transaction someone else would otherwise have funded. It had NO negative coverage.
;;
;;It was reachable all along and nobody had noticed HOW: it reads its subject straight out of
;;(read-msg "exec-code"), so `env-data` IS the fixture and `test-capability` acquires the cap
;;directly. No Talos call, no account, no signing dance.
;;
;;EACH CASE GETS ITS OWN TRANSACTION, and that is not tidiness. A capability acquired by
;;test-capability stays granted for the rest of the tx, so a second acquisition with the SAME
;;arguments returns the cached grant WITHOUT re-running the body -- every rejection after the
;;happy path silently passed as `()`. The first draft of this block did exactly that.
;;==== DALOS-G2a — GAS_PAYER: the payable form IS funded · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== ==============
(print "--- [DALOS-G2a — GAS_PAYER: the payable form IS funded · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(env-chain-data { "gas-limit": 1000, "gas-price": 0.0000001 })
(env-data {"exec-code": ["(ouronet-ns.TS01-C1.something)"]})
(map print
    [
        ;;the HAPPY PATH. Without it every rejection below is equally satisfied by a station that
        ;;refuses to fund anything, which is a broken gas station rather than a safe one.
        (expect "<<DALOS-G2a>> a single ouronet-ns.TS form IS funded"
            true (!= "" (format "{}" [(test-capability (DALOS.GAS_PAYER KST.EMMA 1000 0.0000001))])))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

